    "verification_note": "Per-state gross income limits and asset rules taken from the USDA FNS BBCE States Chart (last updated August 2025) and cross-checked against the CBPP BBCE page. 45 BBCE jurisdictions (43 states + DC + GU + VI). The 7 non-BBCE states are KS, MS, MO, SD, TN, UT, WY. Gross income limit dollar values are NOT stored here; SNAPBBCESource derives them from us_fpl_{fpl_year}.json using SNAP's published rounding ceil(annual_fpl * pct / 100 / 12).",
    "modeling_notes": [
      "net_income_test_applies is true for every jurisdiction. CBPP notes BBCE technically permits states to raise or eliminate the net income limit, but in practice the 100% FPL net test is near-universally applied. Treated here as a modeling assumption.",
      "asset_limit: null = asset/resource test fully waived; a number = state-imposed liquid-asset cap; non-BBCE states carry 3000 (the federal general limit, distinct from the 4500 elderly/disabled limit which is not encoded per-row).",
      "Two-tier states encode the broader (headline) tier; the second tier is recorded in second_tier.",
      "BBCE is conferred by receipt of a non-cash TANF/MOE-funded benefit or service (e.g. an informational brochure, referral, or 1-800 number), not by cash assistance."
    ]
  },

